<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38487" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Prŏconnēsus</span></b> , i,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Προκόννησος</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an island in
				the Propontis</i>, <i>abounding in wine and
			marble</i>, now <i>Marmora</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 7,
			4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 32, 44, §
			151</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Prŏ-connensis</span></b> ,
				e, adj., <i>of
				Proconnessus</i>, <i>Proconnessian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">marmor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 37 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Prŏconnēsĭus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>Proconnessian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ancilla,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 11, 9, § 49</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">marmor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					36, 6, 6, § 47</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">37, 10, 70,
				§ 185</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vitr. 2, 8</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
